          "title": "You'll want to know: ricoverare",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ricoverare — \"to admit to hospital\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Dopo l'incidente l'hanno ricoverato in ospedale. After the accident they admitted him to hospital."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Essere ricoverato is to be in hospital as a patient."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ricoverare is usually traced to Latin recuperāre \"to get back, to regain\" (Lewis & Short). The same verb also means to give shelter, and il ricovero is a shelter."
            }
          ]
        },
